{"id": "unknown-2026-06-03-006", "date": "2026-06-03", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 23, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "UN panel backs Dhaka’s request for 3 more years before LDC graduation", "content": "The UN Committee for Development Policy has expressed a positive position regarding Bangladesh’s request to extend its preparatory period for graduation from the LDC category until November 24, 2029. \nHowever, it emphasised that Bangladesh would need to make significant progress in implementing key domestic reforms to address its existing structural vulnerabilities during this extended period. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/un-panel-backs-dhaka-s-request-for-3-more-years-before-ldc-graduation-310749-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-03-007", "date": "2026-06-03", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 23, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "USTR proposes action against 60 economies in forced labour probes", "content": "USTR has proposed imposing additional duties on imports from 60 economies as their failure to curb trade in goods made with forced labour is unreasonable and restricts US commerce. \nIt would impose 10-per cent duties on imports from the EU, the UK, Canada, Indonesia, Malaysia, Taiwan, Mexico, Pakistan, Argentina, Bangladesh, Cambodia, Ecuador, El Salvador and Guatemala; the rest will face 12.5 per cent. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/ustr-proposes-action-against-60-economies-in-forced-labour-probes-310742-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-03-008", "date": "2026-06-03", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 23, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India launches Mission Senehjori for global Muga silk push", "content": "India has launched Mission Senehjori to transform Assam’s Muga silk sector into a globally recognised luxury textile ecosystem.\nBacked by ₹396-411 crore ($46.6 million–$48.4 million) investment, the initiative focuses on cluster-based development, GI authentication, exports, tourism and higher incomes for silk rearers and weavers across Assam.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-launches-mission-senehjori-for-global-muga-silk-push-310741-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-03-009", "date": "2026-06-03", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 23, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price", "supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": -0.17, "keywords": ["improve", "concerns", "weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Weaker dollar, weather risks lift ICE cotton higher", "content": "ICE cotton futures extended gains as a weaker US dollar improved export competitiveness and weather concerns persisted across key producing regions.\nStrong US export demand and tightening cotton availability in India also supported sentiment.\nThe July 2026 contract settled 0.38 cent higher at 80.54 cents per pound, while traders remained focused on crop conditions in the US and major producers.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/weaker-dollar-weather-risks-lift-ice-cotton-higher-310739-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-03-010", "date": "2026-06-03", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 23, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["sustainable_textile", "supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["uncertainty", "pressure"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "US Section 301 probe puts Indian textile exports under fresh pressure", "content": "USTR’s proposed 12.5 per cent Section 301 tariff has raised uncertainty for India’s textile and apparel exports to the US, especially in apparel, home textiles and MMF products.\nThe move also points towards tighter scrutiny on traceability, sourcing and ESG compliance.\nHowever, India could still strengthen its sourcing position if ongoing India-US trade talks secure favourable tariff treatment.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/us-section-301-probe-puts-indian-textile-exports-under-fresh-pressure-310735-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
